    <div class="flow">
      <p>Not graded. Tap an answer to see if you got it, and read why.</p>
      <Quiz id="quiz-ll" questions={quiz} />
      <div class="remember">
        <p class="note-label">Key takeaways</p>
        <ol>
          <li>Each node holds a value and a reference to the next node. <code>head</code> refers to the first; the last one's next is <code>null</code>.</li>
          <li><code>Node b = a;</code> copies the reference, not the node.</li>
          <li>Traversal follows the links. We cannot jump to a position.</li>
          <li>Insertion and deletion change links, not values. Connect the new node first.</li>
          <li>Singly goes one way, doubly goes both, circular loops back.</li>
          <li>Arrays reach faster. Linked lists edit faster, once you are there.</li>
        </ol>
      </div>
